Substituting $a = r + a$ and $b = a + r$, and rearranging expressions gives:

$a = \frac{-5 + \sqrt{55}}{10},\ m = \frac{-3 + 2a - 4r}{a},\ c = -32r + a^2 + 5b^2 = 2a^2 - 10ar + a^2 + a\sqrt{55} - 6 = \sqrt{55}a - 9,$

with $m = \text{slope of tangent}$, $c = \text{y-intercept of tangent}$, and $r = \text}{radius of circle}.$

The $x$-axis is tangent to the union of a line and a circle. Solve $\sqrt{(x - m)^2 + c^2} - (x - m) - c = 0,$ giving  \[
x = a + \frac{\left(2c + \sqrt{c^2 + 4m^2} \right)}2,\ n = n(m) = a - \frac{ac + cm + 2d}{c^2 + 4m^2}.
\]  The top part of the circle is tangent to the ellipse. We want its top $x =
\[
x = n + r.
